WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.436
A paper market opens between two coloured
platforms.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:08.311
Buyers gather on one side, sellers on the
other, while a single price tag

00:00:08.311 --> 00:00:09.356
floats between them.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.122
The price tag rises. Some buyer tokens
step away.

00:00:19.122 --> 00:00:24.137
In this simple model, a higher price means
fewer items demanded during the

00:00:24.137 --> 00:00:24.522
week.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.220
At the same higher price, more seller
tokens enter.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:39.772
The number of items offered increases, but
the two sides still do not match.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.486
The tokens turn into two moving lines on a
graph.

00:00:49.486 --> 00:00:54.472
Each line connects a price to a quantity,
following its own clearly stated

00:00:54.472 --> 00:00:54.856
rule.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:05.540
Slide the price between the two extremes.
Sometimes buyers want more than

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.022
sellers offer. Sometimes sellers offer
more than buyers want to purchase.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.664
There may be a price where both quantities
match.

00:01:18.664 --> 00:01:23.018
Can you find that price, calculate the
shared quantity, and check both sides

00:01:23.018 --> 00:01:24.022
of the market?
